  "worked_solution": "If $F$ and $G$ are vector fields and $k$ is a constant, then we have the following  linearity properties for divergence:\n\n- $\u2207\\cdot (kF)=k\u2207\\cdot F$\n\n- $\u2207\\cdot (F+G)=\u2207\\cdot F+\u2207\\cdot G.$\n\nFirst, we need to calculate $\u2207\\cdot F.$ In doing so, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\cdot F & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(y\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(2x))+\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}(-{y}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2x)) \\\\  & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2x)-2y\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2x) \\\\  & =-4y\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the linearity properties, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2207\\cdot (F+G) & =\u2207\\cdot F+\u2207\\cdot G \\\\  & =-4y\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2x)+2y\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2x) \\\\  & =-2y\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2x).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
